            0.153,
            0.388,
            0.683,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Cover the square on the hypotenuse using your pieces."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.416,
            0.671,
            0.713
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 3,
              "bbox": [
                0.312,
                0.416,
                0.671,
                0.713
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_13_image_3.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.722,
            0.846,
            0.78
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This shows that if a right triangle has shorter sides of length a and b, and hypotenuse of length c, then the areas of the two smaller squares, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "b ^ { \\bar { 2 } } ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " , add up to the area of the larger square, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "c ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.444,
            0.781,
            0.553,
            0.8
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_13_equation_5.jpg",
          "content": "a ^ { 2 } + b ^ { 2 } = c ^ { 2 } ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.806,
            0.845,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is the famous and fundamental theorem of Baudhāyana on right-angled triangles:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.861,
            0.828,
            0.919
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Baudhāyana’s Theorem on Right-angled triangles:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " If a right-angled triangle has sidelengths a, b, and c, where c is the length of the hypotenuse, then "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "a ^ { 2 } \\stackrel { \\smile } { + } b ^ { 2 } = c ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 8,
